<title>JAPAN: ALPINE SKIING-DOWNHILL TRAINING CANCELLED.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-DOWNHILL TRAINING CANCELLED.</headline>
<dateline>HAKUBA, Japan 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heavy rain and wet snow forced the cancellation on Wednesday of the second day of official training for two women's World Cup downhill races scheduled to begin on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Due to heavy rain and wet fresh snow the course condition does not allow skiing,&quot; said Kurt Hoch, chief race director. &quot;Course preparations are required.&quot;</p>
<p>No decision had yet been made to hold two training runs on Thursday on the course designed for next year's Nagano Winter Olympics, race officials said.</p>
